From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alejandro Corbellini <acorbellini@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 05 Mar 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: rk808: do not arm SLP pin for reset during normal
 operation

rk817_pinctrl_init() selects the "pmic-reset" pinctrl state at the end
of probe, and rk8xx_resume() re-selects it after every suspend/resume
cycle. This keeps the RK817 SLP pin in function 3 (reset mode) during
all normal operation, meaning a glitch on the SLP line triggers a full
PMIC reset.

On some boards (e.g. Miyoo Flip), plugging in a USB charger can induce
enough electrical noise on the SLP line to momentarily trigger such a
reset. The PMIC then powers back on from charger VBUS (ON_SOURCE=0x10),
appearing to the user as a spontaneous reboot.

Fix this by keeping the SLP pin in NULL function during normal operation
(probe and resume). The suspend path already explicitly selects the
sleep pinctrl state, and the shutdown path sets SLPPIN_DN_FUN. To
ensure clean reboots still work (the SoC needs the PMIC to follow its
reset), arm the SLP pin for reset mode in the reboot notifier, which
runs just before the actual system restart.

Signed-off-by: Alejandro Corbellini <acorbellini@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/mfd/rk808.c | 16 +++++++---------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/mfd/rk808.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/rk808.c
@@ -1039,13 +1039,7 @@
 	if (IS_ERR(rk808->pins->reset)) {
 		rk808->pins->reset = NULL;
 		dev_dbg(dev, "no reset-setting pinctrl state\n");
-		return 0;
 	}
-
-	ret = pinctrl_select_state(rk808->pins->p, rk808->pins->reset);
-
-	if (ret)
-		dev_dbg(dev, "failed to activate reset-setting pinctrl state\n");

 	return 0;
 }
@@ -1095,6 +1089,13 @@
 			     value | 0xf0);
 	} else {
 		dev_info(dev, "reboot: not restore POWER_EN\n");
+	}
+
+	/* Arm SLP pin for reset so the PMIC follows the SoC restart */
+	if (data->rk808->pins && data->rk808->pins->p &&
+	    data->rk808->pins->reset) {
+		pinctrl_select_state(data->rk808->pins->p,
+				     data->rk808->pins->reset);
 	}

 	if (action != SYS_RESTART || !cmd)
@@ -1555,9 +1556,6 @@
 			/* pmic need the SCL clock to synchronize register */
 			regmap_read(rk808->regmap, RK817_SYS_STS, &value);
 			mdelay(2);
-			ret = pinctrl_select_state(rk808->pins->p, rk808->pins->reset);
-			if (ret)
-				dev_dbg(dev, "failed to act reset pinctrl state\n");
 		}
 		break;
 	default:
